# Keep the build context small.
#
# Without this, `docker compose build` uploads the entire working directory to
# the daemon on every build — including models/ (~tens of MB of .tflite),
# clips/ and clips-rear-east/ (one full-res JPEG per digging event, unbounded),
# debug_captures/, data/events.db and the whole .git history. None of it is
# COPYed into either image: the Dockerfiles only take *.py, and models/ and the
# clip/data directories are bind-mounted at runtime by docker-compose.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's runtime-artifact entries, with the build-only additions
# (.git, tests, docs) that .gitignore obviously cannot have.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Runtime artefacts — bind-mounted at runtime, never baked into an image
models/
clips/
clips-rear-east/
debug_captures/
data/
notify_workspace/
*.db

# Local config and secrets (mounted read-only at runtime)
config.json
config-*.json
!config-*.example.json
dogwatch-notify.config.json
pipeline/dogwatch-notify.config.json
.ssh
.vision_verify_state.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Tests, samples and docs are not needed in either image.
# NOTE: tests/hardware_smoke_test.py is run on the deployment host by
# bind-mounting it into the container (see the README), not from the image, so
# excluding tests/ here does not break it.
tests/
samples/
*.md
LICENSE

# Editor / OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
